@startuml
Microwave Oven Operation and Control

state MicrowaveOven {
  state Checking
  Checking : do / Check Status

  state Cook
  Cook : do / Run Generator

  state Alarm
  Alarm : do / Display Event

  state Done
  Done : do / Buzzer On for 5 Secs.

  [*] --> Checking

  Checking --> Cook : OK
  Checking --> Alarm : Turntable Fault
  Checking --> Alarm : Emitter Fault

  Cook --> Done : Timeout
  Cook --> Cook : Time

  state Door {
    state Shut
    state Open
  }

  DoorShut : do / Allow DoorOpen
  DoorOpen : do / Allow PlaceFood
  DoorShutItem : do / RequireCloseDoor
  DoorOpenItem : do / RequireCloseDoorAfterPlace

  DoorShut --> DoorOpen : DoorOpened
  DoorOpen --> DoorShut : DoorClosed
  DoorOpen --> DoorOpenItem : FoodPlaced
  DoorShutItem --> DoorShut : FoodPlacedAndDoorClosed
}

Case ID: case_73_oven
Complexity: medium

Requirement:
Oven — Polished Requirement Specification

Functional Requirements
1. The system shall allow the user to open the door whenever it is closed.
2. The system shall allow the user to place food inside or remove it from the microwave when the door is open.
3. The system shall require the user to close the door after placing food inside.
4. The system shall require the user to enter cooking time after the door is closed.
5. The system shall start cooking the food when the user initiates the microwave and continue until the set time is completed.
6. The system shall stop immediately if the door is opened during cooking for safety reasons.
7. The system shall stop when the cooking time ends and allow the user to open the door to remove the food.

state MicrowaveOven {
  state DoorShutItem : do / RequireEnterTime
  DoorShutItem --> Cooking
  Cooking --> Done : Timeout or DoorOpened
  Cooking --> Cooking : Time
}

Case ID: case_69_atm_many_scenarios_6
Complexity: medium

Requirement:
ATM Many Scenarios Scenario 6 — Polished Requirement Specification

Functional Requirements
1. The system shall check if the entered PIN is correct.
2. The system shall ask for the PIN again if it is incorrect.
3. The system shall keep the card for security reasons if the user keeps entering an incorrect PIN or if the card is invalid.
4. The system shall return the card if the user cancels the process at any moment during this stage.
5. The system shall display options for the user to choose from if the PIN is correct.
6. The system shall process the withdrawal request and check if it can approve the transaction.
7. The system shall cancel everything and return the card if the withdrawal request is rejected.
8. The system shall dispense cash, print a receipt, and return the card if the withdrawal request is approved.
9. The system shall stop the operation if it runs out of cash during the process.
10. The system shall reset itself to be ready for the next user after completing or ending the session.

state ATM {
  state Idle
  state EnterPIN
  state InvalidCard
  state IncorrectPin
  state CardKept
  state Options
  state WithdrawalRequest
  state Rejected
  state DispenseCash
  state OutOfCash
  state Completed
}

EnterPIN --> Options : Correct PIN
IncorrectPin --> EnterPIN : Incorrect PIN again
InvalidCard --> InvalidCard : Card Kept
Idle --> EnterPIN : Card Inserted
EnterPIN --> InvalidCard : Invalid Card
EnterPIN --> CardKept : User Cancels

Options --> WithdrawalRequest : User Chooses Withdrawal Option
WithdrawalRequest --> Rejected : Insufficient Funds or Other Issues
WithdrawalRequest --> DispenseCash : Approved Withdrawal Request
DispenseCash --> OutOfCash : No More Cash Available
DispenseCash --> Completed : Cash Dispensed and Receipt Printed
Completed --> Idle
@enduml
